\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Once in royal David's city
\par Stood a lowly cattle-shed,
\par Where a mother laid her baby 
\par In a manger for His bed.
\par Mary was that mother mild,
\par Jesus Christ her little child.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He came down to earth from heaven
\par Who is God and Lord of all,
\par And His shelter was a stable,
\par And His cradel was a stall.
\par With the poor, and mean, and lowly
\par Lived on earth our Saviour holy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And through all His wondrous childhood
\par He would honour and obey,
\par Love, and watch the lowly maiden
\par In whose gentle arms He lay.
\par Christian children all must be
\par Mild, obedient, good as He.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For He is our childhood pattern:
\par Day by day like us He grew;
\par He was little, weak, and helpless;
\par Tears and smiles like us He knew;
\par And He feeleth for our sadness,
\par And He shareth in our gladness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And our eyes at last shall see Him,
\par Through His own redeeming love;
\par For that child so dear and gentle
\par Is our Lord in heaven above;
\par And He leads His children on
\par To the place where He is gone.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

